WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:17.593
The marionette master packed his wagon quickly so he could steal Pinocchio and leave town.

2
00:00:18.373 --> 00:00:23.998
Because he was in a hurry, he threw his money bag, tools, and tent in a pile on

3
00:00:24.038 --> 00:00:25.419
top of Pinocchio's cage.

4
00:00:27.041 --> 00:00:30.804
As the wagon drove on, the heaviest bags fell next to Pinocchio.

5
00:00:31.756 --> 00:00:36.120
By now Pinocchio had stopped crying, though he was still very sad.

6
00:00:37.061 --> 00:00:40.423
He felt the wagon bump and jerk, but could only see bags.

7
00:00:40.443 --> 00:00:45.368
"Hmm, I wonder what's in these bags?"

8
00:00:45.648 --> 00:00:46.248
he thought.

9
00:00:46.268 --> 00:00:50.872
"There must be something here that will help me escape."

10
00:00:51.693 --> 00:00:55.957
He stretched his arm out of the cage as far as it would go and opened the first

11
00:00:56.017 --> 00:00:56.777
bag quietly.

12
00:00:58.118 --> 00:00:59.720
He reached his hand into the bag.

13
00:01:00.888 --> 00:01:03.370
"Oh! This bag is full of coins!

14
00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:06.371
There must be a hundred lire in here!"

15
00:01:07.212 --> 00:01:09.113
He pulled some of the coins into his cage.

16
00:01:09.533 --> 00:01:14.035
Much to his surprise, the coins weren't lire—they were pure gold!

17
00:01:14.055 --> 00:01:17.237
"I'll be rich!

18
00:01:17.997 --> 00:01:19.998
Now I can buy Geppetto a coat!

19
00:01:21.259 --> 00:01:24.941
Oh, but these coins won't help me get out of this cage.

20
00:01:25.862 --> 00:01:27.142
I must keep looking."

21
00:01:28.603 --> 00:01:30.224
He was careful to move quietly.

22
00:01:30.848 --> 00:01:32.489
He reached into the second bag.

23
00:01:32.509 --> 00:01:37.992
"Hmm. This bag has too many different kinds of objects.

24
00:01:38.592 --> 00:01:40.493
I can't tell what any of these are.

25
00:01:41.354 --> 00:01:43.635
Let me pull them out one by one.

26
00:01:45.716 --> 00:01:46.476
A whistle?

27
00:01:47.517 --> 00:01:48.758
No, that won't help.

28
00:01:49.758 --> 00:01:50.419
A spoon?

29
00:01:51.439 --> 00:01:52.740
No, that won't help.

30
00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:53.960
A book?

31
00:01:54.841 --> 00:01:56.462
No, that won't help.

32
00:01:57.562 --> 00:01:58.563
Some matches?

33
00:01:59.783 --> 00:02:02.673
Hmm. I have an idea."

34
00:02:03.614 --> 00:02:05.555
Pinocchio waited for the wagon to stop.

35
00:02:07.536 --> 00:02:12.100
Quickly, he took the book, wrapped it around his leg, and lit the book on fire.

36
00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:14.701
Then, he threw the match into the wagon.

37
00:02:14.721 --> 00:02:16.883
"Help!" he shouted.

38
00:02:16.903 --> 00:02:19.965
"Fire! I'm on fire!"

39
00:02:20.525 --> 00:02:25.448
The marionette master heard Pinocchio cry for help, and he could smell something burning.

40
00:02:27.630 --> 00:02:32.060
He ran to the back of the wagon and began to unpack quickly, trying to find the fire.

41
00:02:32.841 --> 00:02:39.422
When he reached Pinocchio's cage, he grabbed the cage, unlocked it, pulled Pinocchio out, and covered his leg

42
00:02:39.442 --> 00:02:41.163
with a blanket so the fire would stop.

43
00:02:41.183 --> 00:02:45.384
"Look, there's more fire!"

44
00:02:45.944 --> 00:02:47.365
Pinocchio pointed to the wagon.

45
00:02:47.385 --> 00:02:49.045
"Oh no!

46
00:02:49.745 --> 00:02:51.186
My tent is on fire!"

47
00:02:52.026 --> 00:02:55.027
the man screamed, and he hurried to put the fire out.

48
00:02:55.767 --> 00:03:01.831
While the marionette master was trying to save his tent, Pinocchio snuck out from under the blanket and

49
00:03:01.891 --> 00:03:03.392
ran into the nearby woods.

50
00:03:04.713 --> 00:03:09.917
By the time the fire was put out, Pinocchio was long gone, but he could hear the man

51
00:03:09.978 --> 00:03:12.440
yelling in the distance, "No!

52
00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:16.143
Wait! Pinocchio, please come back!

53
00:03:17.064 --> 00:03:18.905
I will make you a star!"

54
00:03:19.826 --> 00:03:22.108
Pinocchio ran and ran and ran.

55
00:03:23.729 --> 00:03:26.812
But no matter how hard he ran, nothing looked familiar.

56
00:03:27.968 --> 00:03:31.190
Pinocchio stopped running and sat down on a stump to think.

57
00:03:32.031 --> 00:03:32.851
"I'm lost!"

58
00:03:33.172 --> 00:03:33.732
he cried.

59
00:03:33.752 --> 00:03:37.615
"I can't find the village and I don't know what to do.

60
00:03:38.555 --> 00:03:40.997
Oh, someone, please help me!"

61
00:03:42.798 --> 00:03:46.601
What Pinocchio didn't realize is that there are many creatures in the woods.

62
00:03:47.681 --> 00:03:51.084
Some are honest and good, and others are greedy.
